This task selects the native direct Walsh inverse of:
Guilherme Beneti Martins, Laurent Mahieu-Williame, Thomas Baudier and Nicolas
Ducros, OpenSpyrit: an ecosystem for open single-pixel hyperspectral imaging,
Optics Express31(10),15599–15614(2023), DOI10.1364/OE.483937.

SPAS reconstruction adaptation: Guilherme Beneti Martins et al., LGPL-3.0.
SPYRIT Walsh ordering: Sebastien Crombez and Nicolas Ducros. The selected
original walsh_hadamard.py file explicitly declares GPLv3, even though the
project-level license is LGPL-3.0; that file-specific notice is preserved and
the combined task implementation is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.
Original source revisions, adaptations and the exact file licenses are indexed
in the maintainer validation record. The reconstruction mathematics is local.

Experimental data: SPIHIM collection, CREATIS/OpenSpyrit authors, acquisition
tomato_slice_2_zoomx1, recorded2021-12-08, configurationv1.2. CC BY4.0.
Data transformations: JSON acquisition identifiers and wavelength calibration
were moved into numeric batch-first NPZ arrays; original raw float64 counts
were preserved exactly. No spatial/spectral resampling or target generation.
Independent method results are not experimental truth. Redistribution of data
must retain the authors' attribution and identify these packaging changes.

